 "notes": "The Blue Hole north of Dahab: a sinkhole over 100 m deep inside the fringing reef, entered from the reef flat on its shore side, with the saddle at about 7 m on the seaward rim and the Arch, a 26 m tunnel with its ceiling at 55 m, through the seaward wall. The Arch depth and length from Wikipedia, its position on the seaward side only approximate. The circuit is the ordinary dive inside the hole; coastline from OpenStreetMap.",
